Subject: Use Gradle project file API for version metadata

Origin: DHI-internal (Gradle compatibility)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/datastax/cass-config-builder.git a5e2fe39a0d39f66ba5deda8336c4df886ee58d9
Regenerate: `sed -i "s/new File('version\\.txt')/file('version.txt')/" build.gradle`
Verify: cmd `./gradlew shadowJar --no-daemon` expect "BUILD SUCCESSFUL"
Forwarded: no (local Gradle compatibility adjustment)
Drop-When: never: required while upstream constructs the version file with the Java File API

This patch switches version.txt access to Gradle's project-scoped file helper so build evaluation uses the project root.

--- a/build.gradle
+++ b/build.gradle
@@ -34,3 +34,3 @@
 description = "Cassandra/DSE Configuration Builder Library"
 group = 'datastax'
-version = "${new File('version.txt').text.trim()}-${getDate()}"
+version = "${file('version.txt').text.trim()}-${getDate()}"
